rset{\\to }{OB}=b=2i+5j+4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =2i+5j+4k-(2i+7j) \\\\  & =-2j+4k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot ⟨0,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268027 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268028 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268029 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268030 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268031 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1041 "selection" 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1104 #edb/ref 17592186268029 13194139533949 true] [17592186268026 1110 #uuid "0c4f24e8-2b08-509d-8782-662496fe1685" 13194139533949 true] [17592186268027 1034 "⟨0,\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}}⟩" 13194139533949 true] [17592186268027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533949 true] [17592186268027 1111 #uuid "1eff147d-7991-5577-941f-dfefef771a2a" 13194139533949 true] [17592186268028 1034 "⟨0,-\\frac